          "key": "cash-basis",
          "name": {
            "en": "Cash accounting scheme",
            "hr": "Postupak oporezivanja prema naplaćenim naknadama"
          },
          "desc": {
            "en": "The supplier accounts for VAT when payment is received rather than\nwhen the invoice is issued, under Article 125.i of the VAT Act. The\nAct requires such invoices to state \"obračun prema naplaćenim\nnaknadama\", which this tag adds as a VAT note."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "extensions": [
    {
      "key": "hr-pass-through",
      "name": {
        "en": "Pass-through Item",
        "hr": "Prolazna stavka"
      },
      "desc": {
        "en": "Kind of pass-through item: an amount the supplier charges together with\ntaxable items that is left out of the VAT base. The amount is a line or a\ncharge of its own, whose VAT combo uses the exempt key and carries this\nextension. The codes are those of the HR tax category table (HR-TB-2) of\nthe Croatian eRačun specification, without the \"HR:\" prefix.\n\nThe consumption tax is a pass-through item too, but it is a percentage of\nthe price of the items it applies to, so it has its own tax category, PP,\ninstead of a code here."
      },
      "sources": [
